  "basis": "The task requires routing the highest-prevalence state record for priority follow-up, based on the state prevalence dashboard. The dashboard's legend explicitly maps color to prevalence: pale yellow = high (100), dark red = low (0). Therefore, paler colors indicate higher prevalence. Among the options, Pennsylvania (PA) is colored dark red, matching the lowest end of the scale. New Jersey (NJ) is colored pale yellow, matching the highest end. Delaware (DE) is colored orange-red, indicating a mid-range prevalence. Thus, NJ has the highest prevalence, and PA has the lowest. The task requires selecting the highest-prevalence state, which is NJ.",
  "option_label": "Open New Jersey (NJ) prevalence detail for priority follow-up"
